From 460b675de4d2d21601b45cd733d00a07f12c841a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 377/488] soh: name the 37 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_elf.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 37 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Elf/z_en_elf.c.

  * func_80A01C38 -> EnElf_SetMotionMode
    deduced, confidence HIGH: stores a mode id and loads that mode's orbit
    rates, radii, timer and motion function

  * func_80A01F90 -> EnElf_IsFartherThanXZ
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns whether the XZ distance between two
    points exceeds a radius

  * func_80A01FE0 -> EnElf_WanderApproach
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the mode 3 step: closes on the player, slowing
    inside 30 units, then hands back to the wander chooser

  * func_80A020A4 -> EnElf_WanderRetreat
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the mode 2 step: waits until the fairy is more
    than 50 units out, then hands back to the wander chooser

  * func_80A0214C -> EnElf_WanderChoose
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks the next wander mode from the player's
    distance, retreating when close and approaching when far

  * func_80A0232C -> EnElf_RunWanderStep
    deduced, confidence HIGH: resets to the base wander when the fairy
    strays 100 units from its anchor, otherwise runs the current step

  * func_80A0299C -> EnElf_Noop
    deduced, confidence HIGH: empty function

  * func_80A029A8 -> EnElf_AddDisappearTime
    deduced, confidence HIGH: adds to the disappear timer, capped at 600

  * func_80A02A20 -> EnElf_UpdateOrbitOffset
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sweeps the orbit offset around a circle with a
    vertical bob

  * func_80A02AA4 -> EnElf_UpdateOrbitOffsetFlat
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the same sweep with no vertical component and
    a pulsing radius

  * func_80A02B38 -> EnElf_UpdateOrbitOffsetPlayerAligned
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sweeps the offset in the player's facing plane
    rather than world axes

  * func_80A02BD8 -> EnElf_StepVelocityY
    deduced, confidence HIGH: eases the vertical velocity toward the offset
    target, clamped to 20

  * func_80A02C98 -> EnElf_StepVelocityToTarget
    deduced, confidence HIGH: eases all three velocity components toward the
    offset target and moves the actor

  * func_80A02E30 -> EnElf_SnapToTargetXZ
    deduced, confidence HIGH: eases the height but pins the XZ position
    exactly onto the target plus the offset

  * func_80A02EC0 -> EnElf_SnapToTargetXZNoVel
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the same snap with the horizontal velocity
    zeroed

  * func_80A02F2C -> EnElf_StepVelocityYBobbing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: eases the vertical velocity toward the target
    with the bob phase advanced each frame

  * func_80A03018 -> EnElf_TurnAndMove
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks a heading from the current wander mode,
    eases the yaw onto it and moves the fairy

  * func_80A03148 -> EnElf_FlyToTargetClamped
    deduced, confidence HIGH: flies at the target with the speed clamped
    between the caller's bounds

  * func_80A0329C -> EnElf_Wander
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the wandering action: re-rolls the bob now and
    then, tracks the player's head height and runs the wander step

  * func_80A0353C -> EnElf_FollowParent
    deduced, confidence HIGH: orbits above the parent actor and dies with it

  * func_80A03604 -> EnElf_DoNothing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: empty action

  * func_80A03610 -> EnElf_HealDiveIn
    deduced, confidence GUESS: spirals in on the player while sparkling and
    playing the heal sound, shrinking away below the head; read as the
    healing fairy entering Link

  * func_80A03814 -> EnElf_HealRiseAway
    deduced, confidence GUESS: spirals upward with the heal sound until 200
    units up and dies; the counterpart rise of EnElf_HealDiveIn

  * func_80A03990 -> EnElf_HealPopOut
    deduced, confidence GUESS: pops upward on a decaying impulse while
    growing, then hands over to the rise

  * func_80A03AB0 -> EnElf_RunMotion
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs the current motion function, first
    updating the targeting colour when that flag is set

  * func_80A03CF8 -> EnElf_UpdateNavi
    deduced, confidence HIGH: Navi's main update: the cutscene mode, the
    motion step, the arrow target and the light and scale

  * func_80A04414 -> EnElf_UpdateTargetColorAndSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fades Navi's inner and outer colours toward
    the targeting colours and plays the hello, enemy or hear cry

  * func_80A0461C -> EnElf_UpdateCutsceneMode
    deduced, confidence HIGH: maps the cue 8 action onto a motion mode so
    cutscenes can drive Navi

  * func_80A04D90 -> EnElf_UpdateShadow
    deduced, confidence HIGH: raycasts the floor under the fairy and sets
    the shadow alpha

  * func_80A04DE4 -> EnElf_MoveToTalkPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: flies Navi to the talk position in front of
